# .NET upgrades

When changing the .NET version (or asked to upgrade/retarget), follow `.cursor/skills/upgrade-dotnet/SKILL.md`. Do not invent the “latest” SDK from memory—resolve it from Microsoft `release-metadata`.

## Must stay in sync

- `src/Directory.Build.props` TFM **and** every hard-coded plugin/build `netN.0` (`*.csproj`, `Notes.txt`, `ClearPluginAssemblies*`)
- `global.json`, `Dockerfile` (`sdk`/`aspnet` tags), `.github/workflows/dotnet.yml`, README “runs on .NET N”
- Rebuild and commit `src/Build/ClearPluginAssemblies.dll` + `.runtimeconfig.json` (RC runtimes need the **exact** framework version, not `N.0.0`)

## Packages

Bump only framework-tied Microsoft refs to the same runtime build (`Microsoft.AspNetCore.*`, `Microsoft.Extensions.Caching.*`, `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite`, `System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager`, Facebook auth package).

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD: bump Mapster because the version looks like a TFM -->
<PackageReference Include="Mapster" Version="10.0.12" />

<!-- ✅ GOOD: align AspNetCore packages with the target runtime -->
<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.NewtonsoftJson" Version="11.0.0-rc.3.26522.148" />
```

After unit tests, smoke with `verify-nopcommerce`.
